📡 Exoplanet Codex — Inference Upgrade Branch
Overview

This branch extends the original Exoplanet Codex pipeline from a classical equivalent-width (EW) + MOOG abundance workflow into a forward-modeling + Bayesian inference framework.

The goal is to move from:

deterministic abundance estimates
to
full posterior distributions of stellar parameters and chemical abundances

while keeping the original EW pipeline fully intact and reproducible.

🧪 Scientific Motivation

Classical stellar abundance pipelines typically follow:

Equivalent width measurement
1D LTE model atmospheres (ATLAS9)
Radiative transfer inversion (MOOG)
Sequential stellar parameter fitting

While robust, this approach has limitations:

Uncertain error propagation (covariances ignored)
Stellar parameters treated as fixed during abundance derivation
EW compression loses spectral information
LTE assumptions not explicitly modeled in uncertainty
Hard to incorporate multi-wavelength datasets (HARPS + HST UV/IR)
